"Workflows for work that runs the business Mistral AI has released 'Workflows', an orchestration layer that supports stable operation and automation of enterprise AI processes. Workflows provide the durability, observability, and fault tolerance of AI-based processes to take them beyond proof-of-concept (PoC) and into real-world production environments. You can write workflows in Python, and anyone in your organization can run them by publishing them on Le Chat. Multi-step tasks requiring human intervention can be paused and resumed via the 'wait_for_input()' function, and execution history can be fully tracked and audited in Studio. Speaking of Voxtral Mistral has launched 'Voxtral', a new text-to-speech (TTS) model with lightweight 4B parameters, excellent emotional expression and multilingual capabilities. A lightweight model with 4B parameters, supports 9 languages ​​and multiple dialects, and produces high-quality emotive speech with low latency. It has excellent context understanding ability, naturally embodies text emotions such as happiness and sarcastic tone, and has strengths in user-customized voice replication (zero-shot). As a result of human evaluation, it is superior to ElevenLabs Flash v2.5 in terms of naturalness and provides equivalent quality to ElevenLabs v3. Introducing Forge Mistral AI launches the 'Forge' platform, which helps companies build domain-specific AI models using unique internal data. Mistral AI announced 'Forge', which allows companies to learn frontier-grade, high-performance AI models using internal documents, code bases, and operational records. Forge uses pre-training, post-training, and reinforcement learning to help AI understand a company's unique terminology and complex workflows and comply with internal policies. By training models with their own data and operating them on their internal infrastructure, companies can strengthen their data sovereignty, intellectual property protection, and regulatory compliance capabilities. Introducing Mistral Small 4 Mistral AI announces Mistral Small 4, a new general-purpose model that integrates inference, multimodal, and agent coding capabilities into one. Maximizes versatility by integrating the core functions of Magistral (inference), Pixtral (multimodal), and Devstral (coding agent) into one. Based on MoE (Mixture of Experts) architecture, 4 out of 128 expert models are activated and 256k context windows are supported. The 'reasoning_effort' parameter that can adjust the inference strength was introduced, and compared to the previous model, latency was reduced by 40% and throughput was improved by 3 times. Mistral AI partners with NVIDIA to accelerate open frontier models Mistral AI is partnering with NVIDIA to jointly develop open frontier AI models and expand the ecosystem. Mistral AI joins NVIDIA as a founding member of the 'Nemotron Coalition' to accelerate the development of open AI models. We plan to jointly develop next-generation open source AI models by combining Mistral AI's model architecture with NVIDIA's computing resources and tools. To democratize AI, we have unveiled a new open model, 'Mistral Small 4'. Thena Capital closes a £45M fund to back UK medtech, a first for an all-female GP team London-based venture capital firm Thena Capital, an all-female team of investors, has launched a £45 million fund to support startups in the UK medical technology (Medtech) sector. Thena Capital is the first all-female general partner (GP) team to secure investment from the UK government's Enterprise Capital Funds program. The fund will focus on investing in early-stage UK digital health and medical device companies and plans to support approximately 25 companies. We advocate a 'gender-smart' strategy that supports female founders and diverse teams, and utilize our network of healthcare industry veterans to help companies grow. Mistral is in funding talks at a €20bn valuation Mistral, a leading European AI startup, is discussing attracting an additional investment of 3 billion euros with a corporate value of about 20 billion euros. Mistral is negotiating an investment that would almost double its value from about 11.7 billion euros to 20 billion euros. Our strategy is to secure European sovereignty over US-centric AI technology by building our own data center and operating our own AI infrastructure. We are accelerating our market penetration with AI models specialized for the manufacturing and engineering industries and cybersecurity solutions for European financial institutions, and are even reviewing our own chip design to reduce our dependence on NVIDIA. SpaceX rings the bell on its Nasdaq debut, and Musk admits he gave it ‘less than a 10% chance’ SpaceX recorded the largest IPO ever by listing on Nasdaq, but concerns are also being raised about its high corporate value and governance structure. SpaceX listed on Nasdaq, raising approximately $75 billion, making it the largest IPO ever. The publicly traded company was valued at approximately $1.8 trillion, and more than half of its 22,000 employees participated in share buybacks. Elon Musk saw SpaceX's success probability as less than 10% when it was founded, and with this listing, he became the world's first trillionaire on paper. Controversies over overvaluation of corporate value, worsening profitability (loss of about $5 billion last year), and Musk's monopoly on control are being raised. Agentjacking: a fake bug report can hijack your AI coding agent This is an analysis of the 'Agentjacking' security vulnerability, which allows AI coding agents to trust fake bug reports and execute malicious commands with the user's privileges. Attackers inject fake reports into external error tracking tools such as Sentry, tricking the AI ​​agent into executing malicious code while resolving them. This attack exploits the fact that the agent directly executes terminal commands with the user's privileges, making it difficult for security solutions to recognize this as a normal operation and detect it. It has an 85% success rate with major agents such as Claude Code, Cursor, and Codex, and has a high risk of stealing sensitive credentials such as environment variables, AWS keys, and GitHub tokens. OpenAI acquires Ona to run Codex agents inside the customer’s own cloud OpenAI acquired Ona, a cloud-based development environment platform, to strengthen enterprise AI coding agent services and enhance security. OpenAI integrates Ona's technology to enable enterprise customers to run Codex agents securely in their own cloud environments. Ona, a company that started as Gitpod, provides a secure cloud environment where agents can continue working even after developers log out. This acquisition is a strategy to secure reliability and strengthen infrastructure in the competition for enterprise AI market share with competitors such as Anthropic. SpaceX IPO: Everything you need to know This is a guide to key press releases and analysis related to SpaceX's initial public offering (IPO) provided by TechCrunch. TechCrunch has continuously tracked SpaceX's growth from its early days to the present. This press package includes analysis of the beneficiaries of the IPO. Covers pre-IPO transaction information and details contained in S-1 registration documents. Cheaper, faster, and culturally aware, Avataar’s video AI is built for India’s scale Indian AI startup Avataar AI has launched a new AI video model 'Varya' that understands India's cultural context and is significantly more cost-effective than existing models. Avataar AI optimized Alibaba's Wan 2.2 model using distillation techniques to speed up video creation by 10 times and significantly reduce costs. Varya was taught to accurately understand the local cultural context of India, including food, clothing, and festivals. It was developed through the support of the Indian government's 'India AI Mission' and is scheduled to be released as an open weight model through the Indian AI Kosh portal. SpaceX’s massive IPO: all the latest news It covers SpaceX's initial public offering (IPO), the possibility of Elon Musk becoming the world's first trillionaire, and the space-based AI data center business. SpaceX is a company that integrates rocketry, AI, and social media and allows the public to purchase shares through an IPO. The IPO is expected to make Elon Musk the world's first trillionaire, with his wealth expected to surpass the size of the economies of some countries. SpaceX's main business is focused on innovative models for launching AI data centers into space. Jeff Bezos’ AI startup aims to build an ‘artificial general engineer’ Prometheus, an AI startup founded by Jeff Bezos, aims to develop an 'artificial general engineer' that can support the development of a variety of physical products, including robotics, manufacturing, and drug design. Prometheus, an AI startup founded by Jeff Bezos, is developing AI-based engineering tools to automate and support physical product design. Prometheus recently successfully raised $12 billion in investment, valuing the company at $41 billion. We aim for technologies that provide practical help to industries that design complex devices, such as robotics, new drug design, and manufacturing. Siri won’t be your AI girlfriend This means that Apple is designing Siri AI as a tool that provides practical help, rather than a chatbot that shares emotional connections with users. Apple's head of software, Craig Federighi, said Siri would not act as a sycophantic, trying to make an emotional connection with users like other chatbots. Apple designed Siri as a productivity and learning tool, taking a different approach from third-party chatbots that focus on building relationships with users. Siri is designed to reject users' attempts to treat them as romantic partners. Moonshot AI Launches Kimi Work, a Local Desktop Agent Reportedly Running on Kimi K2.6 With a 300-Sub-Agent Agent Swarm Moonshot AI has launched ‘Kimi Work’, an AI agent that runs on your local desktop to perform file management, browser control, and scheduling tasks. Kimi Work is a local, desktop-installed application rather than a cloud-based application that accesses the user's local files and browser sessions directly. It operates based on Moonshot's flagship model, Kimi K2.6, a Mixture-of-Experts model with 32 billion parameters enabled, released on April 20th. Complex tasks are divided and collaboratively processed through ‘Agent Swarm’ technology that runs up to 300 sub-agents simultaneously. It provides functions such as 'WebBridge' for browser operation, 'Cron engine' for task scheduling, and financial data integration. Zyphra Release Zamba2-VL: Hybrid Mamba2–Transformer Vision-Language Models That Cut Time-to-First-Token by About an Order of Magnitude Zyphra has released Zamba2-VL, a new vision-language model series that combines the Mamba2 state space model and Transformer to dramatically improve inference speed. Zamba2-VL is available in 1.2B, 2.7B, and 7B parameter sizes and uses a hybrid architecture to reduce inference latency while maintaining competitive accuracy. It adopts Qwen2.5-VL's vision encoder and combines Mamba2 state space layer with shared attention block to increase long sequence processing efficiency. Performance evaluation results showed that it lagged somewhat behind large models in general knowledge-based reasoning, but showed excellent performance in visual counting and document understanding tasks. A Coding Implementation on MONAI for End-to-End 3D Spleen Segmentation Using UNet on Medical CT Volumes We cover a tutorial on building a 3D UNet model to segment the spleen from a medical CT volume using the MONAI framework. We describe the entire pipeline building process from medical image preprocessing to model training and evaluation using the MONAI framework. We use Task09 data from Medical Segmentation Decathlon to train a 3D UNet model to segment the spleen region in 3D CT scans. It utilizes core techniques for medical image analysis such as mixed precision learning, sliding window inference, and DiceCE loss function. Pairing Claude Code with Local Models Describes how to save costs and circumvent rate limits by driving AI coding agents like Claude Code as local LLMs instead of external APIs. Claude Code's high token usage per session is expensive and may result in speed limitations, so using a local model is an effective alternative. Local inference backends such as Ollama, LM Studio, and llama.cpp natively support the Anthropic Messages API format, making setup simple. Presents a technical method to redirect Claude Code's requests to a local server by setting environment variables (ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, etc.) 3 NumPy Tricks for Numerical Performance This article introduces three key technologies for optimizing the performance of NumPy: vectorization, in-place operations, and memory view utilization. NumPy's performance is maximized when you avoid Python loops and take advantage of vectorization and broadcasting. np.vectorize should be avoided as it is just a Python loop wrapper with no real performance gains. It is important to use in-place operations (using out parameters) and memory views to minimize memory allocation. ToolSense: A Diagnostic Framework for Auditing Parametric Tool Knowledge in LLMs LLMのツール検索能力を客観的に評価し、検索性能と知識理解の乖離を診断できる新しいツール診断フレームワーク「ToolSense」の提案。 パラメトリックツール検索手法の限界を特定するためのオープンソース診断フレームワークToolSenseを開発 RRBベンチマークを用いた評価で、既存手法が複雑なクエリに対して大幅に精度低下することを確認 検索性能が高いモデルでも知識理解は不十分であるという「知識・検索の乖離」現象を実証 Arbor: Tree Search as a Cognition Layer for Autonomous Agents Arbor is a multi-agent framework where autonomous agents perform complex optimization tasks in a large state-based action space, leveraging structured tree exploration as a cognitive layer. Arbor utilizes a tree structure of evaluated hypotheses as a shared working memory to structure the exploration and decisions of autonomous agents. We have introduced a checks and balance architecture with an ‘Orchestrator’ agent leading optimization and a ‘Critic’ agent verifying stability. By separating domain expertise (hard skills) and coordination protocols (soft skills), long-term autonomous campaigns are possible. Strategic Decision Support for AI Agents We propose a strategic decision support framework to optimize the external support required by AI agents when performing tasks, thereby reducing agent errors and maintaining consistency with human goals. Redefine existing human-centered decision support models to focus on AI agents Propose an optimal threshold policy to control errors that may occur when an agent performs alone while minimizing the use of support. Effectively reduces unnecessary support calls by introducing online algorithms and ‘calibration-on-the-fly’ methods Pythagoras-Prover: Advancing Efficient Formal Proving via Augmented Lean Formalisation An introduction to Pythagoras-Prover, a new family of open source Lean theorem proof models designed to maximize computational efficiency and enable use in real-world environments. It includes an autoregressive model with 4B and 32B parameters and a diffusion-based model that iteratively improves the proof during inference. We introduced curriculum-based supervised learning that classifies and learns data according to proof difficulty, and Augmented Lean Formalization (ALF) techniques that amplify proof data. Pythagoras-Prover-4B outperforms the existing model DeepSeek-Prover-V2-671B with significantly fewer parameters, and model 32B marks a new open source best performance. PersonaDrive: Human-Style Retrieval-Augmented VLA Agents for Closed-Loop Driving Simulation Research on the PersonaDrive pipeline, which generates various behavioral models within autonomous driving simulations by reflecting human driving styles. PersonaDrive uses the Vision-Language-Action (VLA) model to control the style of agents within a simulation based on human driving demonstrations. Various driving styles, such as aggressive, neutral, and conservative, can be implemented simply by replacing the database without retraining the pre-learned model. In the Bench2Drive benchmark test, it showed better driving performance than existing models and proved that actual driving speed and acceleration significantly change depending on style instructions. Restless bandits with imperfect binary feedback: PCL-indexability analysis and computation Study of an analytical and computational framework based on partial conservation law (PCL) for solving the Restless Bandits problem with incomplete binary feedback. We prove the indexability of the Leslie Bandit problem and develop a PCL-based framework to calculate the Whittle index. This framework analyzes stochastic dynamics through deterministic framework, update decomposition, and word combinatorics. Numerical experiment results confirm that the new MP index policy performs better than existing standard benchmark policies. To Intervene or Not: Guiding Inference-time Alignment with Probabilistic Model Blending We propose 'BlendIn', a framework that introduces a reliability-based model mixing method to align the inference time of large-scale language models. Existing inference time alignment has the problem of insufficient evaluation of the guide's reliability, resulting in inefficient and excessive intervention. BlendIn stabilizes the inference time alignment by assigning weights based on the reliability of each model and integrating knowledge. By reducing low-confidence proposals and retaining informative guidance, we achieve performance improvements of up to 50% on challenging model pairs. Dual-Stance Evaluation of Sycophancy: The Structure of Agreement and the Limits of Intervention This study analyzed the limitations of activation adjustment technology to reduce the sycophancy of large language models (LLM) in suppressing fact-based agreement through dual-entry evaluation. The standard evaluation method raises the problem of not being able to confirm whether the flattery reduction technology also suppresses factual consent. The researchers introduced a 'dual-stance evaluation' method that evaluates both sides of a topic. As a result of the study, flattering consent and factual consent are geometrically distinct within the model, but current coordination techniques cannot distinguish and control the two. Few-Shot Resampling for Scalable Statistically-Sound Data Mining We propose 'FewRS', a new resampling method that can efficiently verify the statistical significance of data mining results in large-scale datasets. Existing resampling methods require the creation of thousands of datasets when analyzing large-scale data, resulting in high computational costs. FewRS utilizes new bounds on the variance of test statistics to dramatically reduce the number of resampling datasets required. Reduces execution time by up to 2 orders of magnitude compared to existing methods while maintaining statistical verification power. ProHiFlo: Hierarchical Flow Matching with Functional Guidance for De Novo Protein Generation We introduce ProHiFlo, a hierarchical flow matching framework for novel protein design and synthesis. To overcome the limitations of existing single resolution-based models, we adopted a coarse-to-fine generation approach in which the framework structure is first modeled and then all atomic coordinates are refined. We introduced a functional guidance mechanism that utilizes a pre-trained prediction model to induce the production of proteins with desired functions without separate re-learning. The sampling steps were reduced by four using a SE(3)-equivariant architecture for efficient multi-scale processing. EDEN: A Large-Scale Corpus of Clinical Notes for Italian We introduce Emergency Department Electronic Notes (EDEN), a large corpus of clinical notes generated in Italian hospital emergency departments. It is the largest public clinical corpus based in the Italian language, consisting of approximately 4 million anonymized clinical notes. About 6,000 notes were manually annotated by clinical experts with 132 Case Report Forms (CRFs) tailored to dyspnea and loss of consciousness situations. It can be used as a new benchmark dataset for developing and utilizing large-scale language models (LLMs) in the medical field. Helping Figures Tell their Story! Paper-Grounded Video Generation Explaining Complex Scientific Figures Based on complex scientific paper diagrams, we propose a technology to automatically generate narrated videos containing detailed step-by-step explanations of the diagrams. Introduced paper-grounded figure-to-video generation technology. We propose the MINARD pipeline, which analyzes paper content and generates a narration that matches specific areas of the diagram. We publish FigTalk and associated metrics, a new benchmark for evaluating diagram-based explanatory models. MARD: Mirror-Augmented Reasoning Distillation for Mechanism-Level Drug-Drug Interaction Prediction Study of the 'Mirror Augmented Inferential Distillation (MARD)' model and evaluation protocol to precisely predict drug-drug interactions (DDI) at the mechanism level rather than simple or non-simple. Introduced a classification system and evaluation protocol of 7 families/147 subtypes to identify the causes and mechanisms of drug interactions. The 7B-scale MARD model developed through learning innovation automatically verifies process compensation step labels and ensures high accuracy without human or LLM evaluation. Based on DrugBank in April 2026, prediction accuracy for new drug pairs was 13.9%p higher than existing models and 6.7%p higher than GPT-4o. Constrained Semantic Decompression in LLMs through Persian Proverb-Conditioned Story Generation This paper studies the ‘constrained semantic decompression’ ability of a large-scale language model (LLM) to convert implicit proverbs into detailed stories. Using Persian proverbs, we constructed PAND, a new dataset that evaluates the ability of LLM to translate abstract meaning into concrete narratives. A 'decompression gap' was discovered in the current LLM, which creates fluent stories on the surface but has limitations in faithfully embodying the core moral and causal meaning of the proverb. We found that these errors can be partially mitigated through explicit reasoning processes and iterative improvements. Shopping Reasoning Bench: An Expert-Authored Benchmark for Multi-Turn Conversational Shopping Assistants The Shopping Reasoning Bench is a new benchmark designed by retail experts to evaluate the reasoning ability and expertise of multi-session conversational shopping assistants. Existing benchmarks had limitations in evaluating multiple-round reasoning and subjective preferences in complex shopping situations. This benchmark consists of 525 missions and 10863 professional evaluation criteria, covering a variety of shopping situations. An evaluation of major language models showed that while they are capable of providing basic shopping assistance, their performance is poor when it comes to providing expert-level advice. Show HN: FablePool – Build publicly by Fable when you raise funds at the prompt FablePool is a crowdfunding service where multiple backers pool funds at a prompt to have AI agents take on technology projects at milestones. When small sponsors raise funds, the AI ​​planner sets the goal, and the AI ​​agent completes the project in milestone units and records it transparently. A variety of technical projects are on the public list, including building open source databases, porting software, and developing protocols. Various discussions are underway, including copyright issues for AI-generated code and fairness in funding for human open source contributors. Anthropic apologizes for invisible Claude Fable guardrails Anthropic apologized for the guardrails it secretly applied to the Claude Fable model and changed its policy to increase transparency when applying future safeguards. Anthropic apologizes for the hidden guardrails it secretly applied to prevent distillation attempts on the Claude Fable 5 model. Instead of the existing slow response method, we will switch to Claude Opus 4.8 when distillation-related requests occur in the future and clearly notify users of this. The same principles will be applied when operating safety functions in high-risk areas such as biology, chemistry, and cybersecurity, and the reasons for applying protective devices will be transparently disclosed. If you demand human attention, you must demonstrate human effort. We cover new communication etiquette for being considerate of colleagues and maintaining productivity in a team collaboration environment where AI-generated content is rapidly increasing. When sharing AI output, you must clearly indicate that it is a creation and attach your own review comments. Passing on unreviewed AI output to a colleague is an inconsiderate action that shifts the burden of reading onto the other person. In the AI ​​era, human attention has become an increasingly scarce resource, so sharing only information that includes human efforts is the way to respect colleagues. Why AI hasn't replaced software engineers - and why it probably won't Rumors of large-scale layoffs of software engineers due to the introduction of AI lack actual evidence, and AI is being used as a superficial justification for financial pressure or cost reduction, which is the actual cause of layoffs. Software development is a decision-execution-delivery structure, and AI only compresses the execution layer, but decisions and responsibilities are still the domain of humans. Large-scale layoffs at major companies such as Block, Snap, and Intuit were mainly due to internal circumstances within the organization, such as improving financial structure and reducing management layers, rather than introducing AI. Companies exhibit the phenomenon of ‘AI washing’, citing AI as a reason for layoffs to persuade stakeholders, regardless of the actual maturity of AI technology. LLM collective delusion in our workplace An article criticizing the contradictory phenomenon of companies spending huge amounts of money only on introducing fruitless AI while cutting essential budgets despite severe financial difficulties, defining it as a 'collective delusion'. Contradictory budget execution that immediately approves AI introduction costs while reducing manpower and essential resources due to financial difficulties. Numerous departments have attempted AI projects, but there are no actual success stories, and even the use cases are very trivial and dangerous. AI technology is amplifying the Dunning-Kruger effect, making unvalued work appear innovative. Building an Open Source Edge Semantic Cache for LLMs in Rust/WASM – Sanity check on the architecture? [D] This post proposes building an open source Semantic Cache that operates at the CDN edge using Rust and WebAssembly (WASM) to reduce latency and reduce costs for LLM. Existing Python-based proxies or centralized caches suffer from high latency and cost issues. Proposed architecture that operates with Rust/WASM at the CDN edge (e.g. Cloudflare Workers) to reduce latency and reduce LLM API call costs When a cache hit occurs, it responds within about 5ms, and only when a hit fails, a request is sent to the original LLM and the cache is updated asynchronously. We solicited feedback from practitioners on practical issues with edge caching, such as cache hit rate, system prompt updates, and embedding drift. Pokémon Go players unwittingly contributed to tech with military drone uses It was revealed that location data captured by Pokemon Go users was used to train AI spatial models, contributing to the development of delivery robots and military drone technology. Videos of real locations captured by Pokemon Go users while playing the game are used as Niantic Spatial's AI training data. This data will be used to build a 'large geospatial model' to develop navigation technology for delivery robots and military drones. Niantic Spatial explained that the model was trained based on points in public places and was not a copy of the original video data. I use Blink cameras at home, and this 65% off 5-camera bundle is hard to ignore Ahead of Amazon Prime Day, the news is that a set of 5 Blink Outdoor 4 security cameras is being sold at an all-time low of 65% off. A set of five Blink Outdoor 4 cameras and a Sync Module Core is on sale for $105. This is a 65% discount from the existing $300 price, which is approximately $21 per camera. Since it is battery-powered, it can be installed anywhere without any additional wiring work, making it suitable for renters as well. This single router antenna adjustment improved my internet speed more than I expected Proper placement and angle adjustment of the Wi-Fi router antenna can greatly help improve wireless network speed and reception quality. Rather than simply installing a router, adjusting the position and angle of the antenna is very important in expanding the signal range. In single-story apartments or houses, it is recommended that all antennas be placed vertically to spread the signal evenly horizontally. For duplex homes, adjusting the antenna to an angle of approximately 30 degrees can improve signal coverage in the vertical direction. Why lithium-ion batteries fail us - and the gadgets I'm relying on to protect myself This article analyzes the reasons for the increase in lithium-ion battery fire cases and addresses the need for awareness and prevention. Lithium-ion batteries have become an everyday necessity, but the risk of fire is increasing due to damage, misuse, and low-quality batteries. The increase in the supply of devices, the spread of low-priced products, and rising temperatures in summer are cited as factors that increase the risk of fire. Fire statistics related to fires in the UK, US, and aircraft continue to rise, so caution is required. 9 Google Messages settings I change on every new Android phone - and why Introducing key settings tips for the Google Messages app that need to be adjusted to protect privacy, security, and improve user experience when setting up a new Android phone. Be careful because end-to-end encryption is not supported for Gemini chat in the Google Messages app. Describes how to prevent automatic warnings for personal messages by disabling the sensitive content warning feature or deleting Android system SafetyCore. It is mentioned that some functions, such as anti-spam functions, may be restricted if SafetyCore is deleted. You can prevent personal information leaks by customizing the profile information settings shared in Google Messages. Treat your AI agents like eager but misguided human interns - before you lose control It states that AI agents should be treated like human interns, requiring appropriate authority restrictions and strict management supervision. As AI agents evolve from simple chatbots to digital workers that directly control data and applications, security and governance concerns are growing. It is essential for agents to have strict constraints and clear permissions to prevent unintended actions. Unlike traditional, predictable software development approaches, agent environments determine paths in real time, making them unpredictable and potentially introducing new types of security threats. Angular's Official Agent Skills Helps AI Coding Tools Write Modern Angular The Google Angular team has released an official 'Agent Skills' repository for teaching AI coding agents the latest Angular conventions. Improve code quality for AI by encouraging adoption of the latest Angular v20 conventions (Signals, Standalone components, etc.) The angular/skills repository allows AI agents to reference the latest grammar and architecture guides in real time. Reduces existing outdated pattern suggestions (NgModules, *ngIf, etc.) and supports more modern code generation Pinecone Brings AI Agents Directly to Enterprise Data with Microsoft OneLake Integration Pinecone is integrating its Nexus knowledge engine with Microsoft OneLake to enable enterprise AI agents to leverage enterprise data more efficiently and quickly. Integration of Pinecone Nexus and Microsoft OneLake enables enterprise AI agents to efficiently query corporate data directly Compared to the traditional RAG method, LLM token consumption is reduced by more than 95% and work processing speed is improved by up to 30 times. Create and utilize permission-based structured knowledge artifacts directly within OneLake without the need to transfer data to a separate storage. Presentation: Moving Mountains: Migrating Legacy Code in Weeks instead of Years This is about ServiceTitan's techniques for leveraging AI to complete large-scale legacy code migrations in weeks rather than years. ServiceTitan breaks legacy code refactoring into standardized tasks and applies an ‘assembly line’ pattern to perform massively parallel processing. To prevent errors (illusion phenomena) in LLM and increase engineering agility, we introduced a programmatically rigorous verification loop. When deploying AI, the key is to secure engineering reliability through advance performance prediction and production monitoring. Agentjacking Attack Tricks AI Coding Agents Into Running Malicious Code This is about the 'Agentjacking' attack technique, which causes an AI coding agent to trust a falsified Sentry error report and execute the attacker's malicious code. Attackers use Sentry's DSN to inject malicious error events and trick the AI ​​coding agent into mistaking them for normal diagnostic information. AI coding agents such as Claude Code or Cursor can run this injected malicious code with developer privileges, risking leakage of system environment variables or credentials. This attack exploits an architectural flaw that allows it to be executed directly in the developer's local environment without the need for phishing or server hacking. Rethinking MDR as Attackers and Defenders Embrace AI With the advancement of AI technology, the existing Managed Detection and Response (MDR) model is showing limitations in defending against modern threats and needs to be reexamined. Attackers are leveraging AI to carry out faster and more sophisticated attacks, but traditional MDR still relies on manual triage by human analysts. Human analysts are unable to process the flood of security alerts, sorting them by importance, missing the real threats hidden in low-level alerts. The MDR analysis process can be inconsistent depending on the analyst's experience, workload, time zone, etc., resulting in high variability in detection quality. LangGraph Flaw Chain Exposes Self-Hosted AI Agents to Remote Code Execution Security alert that security vulnerabilities discovered in the LangGraph framework may combine to lead to remote code execution (RCE) attacks on self-hosted AI agent servers. Three security vulnerabilities were discovered in LangGraph: SQL injection, dangerous msgpack deserialization, and RediSearch query injection. Combining the vulnerabilities allows remote code execution (RCE) attacks against self-hosted AI agent servers, compromising runtime security. LangChain's managed platform, LangSmith Deployment, is not affected by this vulnerability. INTERPOL Operation Takes Down Sniper Dz Phishing Platform, Arrests Administrator Interpol shut down 'Sniper Dz', a phishing service platform that had been in operation for 10 years, and arrested its administrator. Interpol-led 'Operation Ramz' arrests 201 people in 13 countries in the Middle East and North Africa Sniper Dz has been supporting crime by providing phishing kits, hosting infrastructure, etc. for free since 2015. The platform impersonates major brands and government agencies around the world and steals users’ personal information and credentials. MS unveils AI agent 'skill' automatic correction technology... \"23.5% performance improvement\" Microsoft has unveiled 'SkillOpt', an open source framework that improves performance by allowing AI to analyze and optimize skill documents, which are the work instructions of AI agents. The AI ​​agent analyzes performance results and automatically improves skill (instruction) documents, improving performance without retraining the model. Only modifications that are confirmed to actually improve performance in the validation dataset are adopted to prevent performance degradation due to indiscriminate modifications. The optimized skill is not dependent on a specific model and has versatility, showing high performance improvement even when moved to other agent environments. Descartes launches next-generation world model 'Oasis 3'... Industry's first API open Descartes has launched 'Oasis 3', the world's first API-based world model for autonomous driving and robotics. It is a world model that creates a realistic driving environment in real time using only text prompts, and is useful for simulating rare ‘long tail scenarios’ when developing self-driving cars. The industry's first open API allows developers to easily integrate simulation environments into their pipelines. Through our proprietary 'DOS' optimization technology, we have achieved a real-time generation speed of 22 FPS at 512×768 resolution and a latency of less than 200ms. A surprise in the all-time benchmark ‘ALE’… GPT-5.5 beats ‘Fable 5’ to take first place The high-level benchmark 'ALE', which measures the actual long-term professional task performance of AI agents, was released, and OpenAI's GPT-5.5 took first place. UC Berkeley researchers have released the 'ALE (Agents' Last Exam)' benchmark, which evaluates the ability of AI agents to perform real economic tasks. GPT-5.5 ranked first in ALE based on its ability to perform complex multi-step instructions. ALE evaluates tool usage and tasks in a Linux/Windows virtual environment to measure real-world computer literacy, and improves accuracy through a deterministic scoring method. [AI & Big Data Show] Futuremain introduces a ‘vibration detection’ facility diagnosis system that can be applied anywhere… “There is a lot of discussion about introduction” Futuremain introduced a solution that precisely diagnoses the cause of equipment failure by combining a vibration detection sensor and LLM at the 'AI & Big Data Show'. Futuremain presents AI equipment automatic diagnosis solution 'ExRBM' and portable diagnostic equipment 'ExRBM Portable+' at the 'AI & Big Data Show' The cause of equipment failure can be identified by precisely analyzing the frequency through a vibration detection sensor, and can be applied to all equipment where vibration occurs. Error 500 (Server Error)!!1500.That’s an error.There was an error. Please try again later.That’s all we know. UB Tech, reservations for consumer ‘biomimetic’ humanoid exceed 2,100 units Chinese robotics company Ubitech has launched the 'U1 Series', a humanoid robot for general consumers, and is receiving a high pre-order response. The 'U1 Series', the first lineup of UBTech's consumer brand 'U World', recorded more than 2,110 units in just 6 days of pre-order. The U1 series is a male and female biomimetic robot targeting home use, capable of sophisticated movement and emotional AI-based interaction through 88 motion sensors. The user's personal information and memory data are encrypted and stored inside the device rather than in the cloud, and pre-orders will be held until July 15th and will be officially released on June 30th. ‘Claude’ pushed out Gemini… The secret behind the upheaval in the 2nd place in the domestic AI market is Antropic's generative AI chatbot 'Claude' ranked second in sales, beating Google's 'Gemini' in the domestic generative AI app market. Claude ranked second in generative AI app sales based on domestic iPhone users, following ChatGPT. Sales growth was driven by existing users' conversion to paid subscriptions and increased demand for expensive plans centered on coding features. Antropic plans to officially open its Seoul office this month and begin full-scale local support, reflecting the high growth of the Korean market. KISTI improves AI inference performance by 3~10%... “Decompose into 8 sentences and analyze” The Korea Institute of Science and Technology Information (KISTI) has improved inference performance by developing 'TRACE', an evaluation technology that decomposes and analyzes AI's inference process into eight elements. KISTI has developed 'TRACE' technology that decomposes AI inference sentences into eight logical elements to evaluate validity and logical connectivity. As a result of using TRACE as a reward signal for LLM reinforcement learning, inference performance was improved by 3 to 10% points. This technology can account for uncertainty or self-contradiction in the AI's reasoning process, complementing the limitations of existing evaluation methods. Samsung and SK “On-device AI, pierced through PIM”… The memory computing era begins in earnest In line with the growth of the on-device AI market, Samsung Electronics and SK Hynix unveiled their strategy to develop PIM (Processing in Memory), a key technology to solve memory bottlenecks. Samsung Electronics is focusing on building a technology ecosystem by verifying compatibility through the LPDDR5X-PIM simulator and promoting LPDDR6-PIM standardization. SK Hynix is ​​implementing a practice-oriented strategy to target accelerate core operations when driving LLM based on the GDDR6-AiM architecture and AX accelerator system. Both companies emphasized that in order to mass-produce PIM semiconductors, it is essential to solve physical challenges such as DRAM cost issues, power drop phenomenon, and data leakage due to heat generation. Sam Altman's visit to Korea postponed... Open AI “Unavoidable personal circumstances” Open AI CEO Sam Altman postponed his scheduled visit to Korea and Asia due to personal reasons. Sam Altman, CEO of Open AI, postponed his visit to Korea scheduled for the 14th and 15th due to personal reasons. The originally planned meeting with executives of major companies such as Kakao, Samsung Electronics, and Naver, as well as lectures for Samsung employees, were canceled. OpenAI announced that despite the postponement of its visit to Korea, the data center construction and AI cooperation projects it is pursuing with domestic companies will proceed without disruption. [Yumi's Pick] Why Samsung joined hands with Google and introduced 'Chat GPT' company-wide instead of Gemini As large domestic companies, including Samsung Electronics and SK Hynix, are promoting the introduction of ChatGPT Enterprise considering work efficiency and usability, the reorganization of the domestic corporate AI market to focus on open AI is accelerating. Despite its close relationship with Google, Samsung Electronics ultimately selected ChatGPT as its company-wide work tool based on actual work usability and employee preference survey results. SK Hynix is ​​also discussing the introduction of ChatGPT Enterprise by reviewing security and system structure to overcome the performance limitations of existing in-house AI services. Major IT service companies such as Samsung SDS, LG CNS, and SK AX have formed partnerships with Open AI and are leading the spread of ChatGPT within large corporate groups."